{
  "titulo": "New Ballard Score (edad gestacional)",
  "descripcion": "Estima la edad gestacional del recién nacido con seis signos de madurez neuromuscular y seis de madurez física, de −10 a 50 puntos (20 a 44 semanas). Es la versión de 1991 de la escala de Ballard, ampliada a los prematuros extremos y validada en 578 recién nacidos, con una correlación de 0,97 con la edad gestacional por fecha de última regla confirmada por ecografía.",
  "referencias": [
    {
      "titulo": "Ballard JL, Khoury JC, Wedig K, Wang L, Eilers-Walsman BL, Lipp R. New Ballard Score, expanded to include extremely premature infants. J Pediatr 1991;119(3):417-23.",
      "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/1880657/",
      "texto": "For infants less than 26 weeks of gestational age, the greatest validity (97% within 2 weeks of C-GLMP) was seen when the examination was performed before 12 hours of postnatal age."
    },
    {
      "titulo": "Moore KA, et al. Gestational age assessment in malaria pregnancy cohorts: a prospective ultrasound demonstration project in Malawi. Malar J 2013;12:183.",
      "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23734718/",
      "texto": "Several suggest, as did the present one, that the Ballard score overestimated the gestational age in preterm infants leading to an underestimation of the percentages of preterm infants."
    },
